  "description": "issue #682 (slice I3): two `when \"start\"` handlers registered in sequence fire in REGISTRATION ORDER (spec/interaction-events.md's \"Time, ticks, and handlers\": pending `when` events fire in registration order). Because `\"start\"` is already being delivered in a batch run, each handler fires immediately on its own registration, so handler `a` (registered first) completes entirely before handler `b` is registered and fires: the sequence is register-a (seq 0-1) → fire-a (seq 2-4) → register-b (seq 5-6) → fire-b (seq 7-9). The single append-only registration list gives one total order across handlers, the stable order same-tick dispatch (#686/I7) builds on; this slice keeps that order observable without owning cross-handler same-tick timing.",
